        place. This is the fastest way to get an overview of the entire laboratory
        layout.
      videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 9b5a1abda84e6dc46a8471d2832fcbba, type: 3}
    - title: How to rotate the view (2)
      content: In addition to turning physically, you can use the joystick on the
        right controller to rotate your view. This allows you to turn the camera
        without moving your body.
      videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 28a0b8735faa271449d918847937ab18, type: 3}
    - title: How to move (1)
      content: To move forward, backward, left, or right, simply use the joystick
        on the left controller.
      videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: d8e81b8a5d7104c41be436eb8bc9afab, type: 3}
    - title: How to move (2)
      content: Additionally, you can use the laser on the right controller to point
        at a specific location, then press the side button (Grip button) to move
        there.
      videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: d938feca435c1794c917cf8ce6207a54, type: 3}
  - tutorialName: Tutorial_Microscope_OutSide
    nodes:
    - title: Enable the light source
      content: Point at the microscope and press the B button on the Right Controller.
        This turns on the microscope's light source. If you don't do this, you won't
        be able to see any image in Observation Mode.
      videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: b16f5e1691b26d0408c4031dd415b1a0, type: 3}
    - title: Collect a sample
      content: Point at a sample and press the Right Trigger. You will see a preview
        image of the sample in the bottom-right corner of your VR headset.
      videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 2c466f004effeda45811864b1c616433, type: 3}
    - title: Switch to another sample
      content: To observe a different sample, simply walk over to the new sample,
        point at it, and press the Right Trigger to collect it. An important thing
        is that we need to press the Right Trigger to remove the sample from the
        microscope, so that we can place the new samle on it.
      videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 317e27fb8d78f944197e4ea861fc2eba, type: 3}
    - title: Adjust external light source
      content: While pointing at the microscope, hold down the X button on the Left
        Controller and simultaneously move the Right Stick. This adjusts the light
        source, which changes the brightness of the sample when you are in Observation
        Mode.
      videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 6a414c6201016034cb1ddb2b5b21a159, type: 3}
    - title: Enter Observation Mode
      content: 'Point at the microscope and press the Left Trigger to perform the
        following actions in order: 1. First Press: Places your selected sample onto
        the stage. 2. Second Press: Locks your view to the microscope. 3. Third Press:
        Enters Observation Mode.'
      videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 3ac18192c0d15734390bbbb060c61797, type: 3}
  - tutorialName: Tutorial_Microscope_InSide
    nodes:
    - title: Exit Observation Mode
      content: Press the Left Trigger to exit Observation Mode.
      videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: c365dc31d22ae724e9805fed230e3af5, type: 3}
    - title: Move Specimen
      content: While in Observation Mode, use the Left Stick (Up, Down, Left, Right)
        to move the specimen image accordingly within your field of view.
      videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 08e6a155e5ee58a4dbd0386b3ba87a91, type: 3}
    - title: Adjust Focus / Brightness
      content: 'To adjust settings while in Observation Mode, hold the X button on
        the Left Controller and use the Right Stick: - Move the stick Left/Right:
        Adjusts the Focus. - Move the stick Up/Down: Adjusts the Brightness inside
        the microscope.'
      videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: d4d2d88de918abc408d66b83a7cea32c, type: 3}
    - title: Adjust Focus / Brightness
      content: 'To adjust settings while in Observation Mode, hold the X button on
        the Left Controller and use the Right Stick: - Move the stick Left/Right:
        Adjusts the Focus. - Move the stick Up/Down: Adjusts the Brightness inside
        the microscope.'
      videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 73c9a41ac6bfd0341a4e599058302949, type: 3}
    - title: Adjust focus until the image is clear
      content: To get a clear image, you must continuously adjust the focus until
        it reaches the 'sweet spot' (critical point), at which point the image will
        become sharp.
      videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: a55234d6a3841274ba099052d463e9c0, type: 3}
    - title: Switch between Coarse and Fine Focus
      content: 'Press the Right Stick (click inward) to toggle between Coarse and
        Fine Focus: - Coarse Focus: Allows for rapid focal changes. - Fine Focus:
        Allows for precise, minute adjustments to sharpen the detail.'
      videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 9b0e49d7843504d4198c249bf1c3cd64, type: 3}
    - title: Switch Objective Lens
      content: Press the B button on the Right Controller to switch to a different
        objective lens, which will provide a different level of magnification.
      videoClip: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 971f7be4e05d11041a3ccbcbcd7a053b, type: 3}
  microscope: {fileID: 0}
  player: 0
  level: 0
  page:
  - {fileID: 0}
  - {fileID: 0}
  tutorialButton: {fileID: 1294495120250449003}
